---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import CTASection from '../components/CTASection.astro';
import Disclaimer from '../components/Disclaimer.astro';
import AuthorByline from '../components/AuthorByline.astro';
import { BUSINESS, MEDICARE_2026 } from '../data/site';

const title = 'Does Medicare Plan G Pay for Eye Exams, Hearing Aids or Dental Care?';
const seoTitle = 'Plan G: Eye Exams, Hearing Aids and Dental';
const description = 'Original Medicare does not cover routine eye exams, hearing aids or most dental care, and Medigap Plan G does not add them. Here is what is covered.';

const faqs = [
  { q: 'Does Medicare pay for routine eye exams?', a: 'No. Medicare does not cover routine eye exams for glasses or contact lenses. It does cover a yearly glaucoma screening for people at high risk, and cataract surgery that implants an intraocular lens.' },
  { q: 'Does Medicare cover hearing aids?', a: 'No. Original Medicare does not cover hearing aids or exams to fit them. It does cover diagnostic hearing and balance exams when a doctor orders them to see if you need medical treatment.' },
  { q: 'Does Medicare cover dental care?', a: 'In most cases no. Medicare generally does not cover cleanings, fillings, extractions or dentures. It may cover dental services directly tied to a covered medical treatment, such as an exam before a heart valve replacement.' },
];

const schema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@graph': [
    {
      '@type': 'WebPage',
      '@id': `${BUSINESS.url}/does-medicare-plan-g-cover-eye-exams-hearing-aids-dental#webpage`,
      name: title,
      description,
      about: [{ '@type': 'Thing', name: 'Medigap', sameAs: 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Medigap' }],
      speakable: { '@type': 'SpeakableSpecification', cssSelector: ['.lead', 'h2'] },
    },
    { '@type': 'FAQPage', mainEntity: faqs.map((f) => ({ '@type': 'Question', name: f.q, acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: f.a } })) },
  ],
};
---

<BaseLayout title={title} seoTitle={seoTitle} description={description} schema={schema}>
  <PageHero
    title={title}
    breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Medicare Plans', href: '/services' }, { label: 'Medicare Supplement Insurance (Medigap)', href: '/services/medicare-supplement' }, { label: 'Eye exams, hearing aids and dental' }]}
  />

  <article class="py-14 lg:py-18">
    <div class="container-narrow prose prose-lg max-w-none prose-headings:font-display prose-headings:text-crst-primary prose-a:text-crst-accent">

      <div class="not-prose mb-8 rounded-xl border-l-4 border-crst-gold bg-navy-50 p-5">
        <p class="text-navy-800 leading-relaxed m-0">
          Not on its own. Original Medicare does not cover routine eye exams, hearing aids or most dental care, and a Medigap plan such as
          Plan G helps with Original Medicare’s costs rather than adding those benefits.
        </p>
      </div>

      <p class="lead text-xl text-navy-700">
        This is one of the most common surprises for people who buy a Medigap plan. Here is what Original Medicare does and doesn’t cover
        for your eyes, ears and teeth, and what Plan G adds.
      </p>
      <p class="text-sm text-navy-500 -mt-2">
        Written by <a href="/about">Jim Farnham, MS, MBA</a> — Licensed Agent / Insurance Broker (NY license {BUSINESS.nyLicense}).
      </p>

      <h2>Eye care</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Routine eye exams are not covered.</strong> Medicare doesn’t cover routine eye exams (sometimes called “eye refractions”) for eyeglasses or contact lenses.</li>
        <li><strong>A yearly glaucoma screening is covered for people at high risk</strong> (for example, if you have diabetes or a family history of glaucoma), once every 12 months, when an eye doctor legally allowed to do the test in your state does or supervises it.</li>
        <li><strong>Cataract surgery that implants an intraocular lens may be covered.</strong> Part B also covers one pair of eyeglasses with standard frames, or one set of contact lenses, after each cataract surgery that implants an intraocular lens. Other glasses and contact lenses are generally not covered.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Details: Medicare.gov on <a href="https://www.medicare.gov/coverage/eye-exams-routine" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">routine eye exams</a>,
        <a href="https://www.medicare.gov/coverage/glaucoma-screenings" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">glaucoma screenings</a> and
        <a href="https://www.medicare.gov/coverage/eyeglasses-contact-lenses" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">eyeglasses and contact lenses</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Hearing</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Hearing aids are not covered,</strong> and neither are exams to fit them.</li>
        <li><strong>Diagnostic hearing and balance exams are covered</strong> under Part B when your doctor or other health care provider orders them to find out if you need medical treatment.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Details: Medicare.gov on <a href="https://www.medicare.gov/coverage/hearing-aids" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">hearing aids</a> and
        <a href="https://www.medicare.gov/coverage/hearing-balance-exams" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">hearing and balance exams</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Dental</h2>
      <p>
        In most cases Medicare doesn’t cover dental services such as routine cleanings, fillings, tooth extractions, dentures or implants.
        It may cover dental services you get as part of certain covered medical treatment, when the dental service is linked to the success of
        that treatment, for example an oral exam and dental treatment before a heart valve replacement or an organ or kidney transplant. See
        <a href="https://www.medicare.gov/coverage/dental-services" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">Medicare.gov on dental services</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>What Plan G adds</h2>
      <p>
        For the services Original Medicare does cover, Plan G pays the Part B coinsurance or copayment. For example, after you have paid the
        Part B deductible ({MEDICARE_2026.partBDeductible} in {MEDICARE_2026.year}), a covered glaucoma screening or a covered diagnostic
        hearing exam leaves you owing the Part B deductible, but not the 20% coinsurance. For care Original Medicare doesn’t cover, Plan G
        does not pay. The full list of what it does pay is in
        <a href="/what-medigap-plan-g-does-not-cover">what Plan G does not cover</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Ways to cover routine eye, hearing and dental care</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>A stand-alone plan.</strong> Dental, vision and hearing plans are sold separately from Medicare. Coverage and value vary by plan, so match one to what you actually expect to use. See <a href="/services/dental-vision-hearing">dental, vision, hearing and hospital coverage</a>.</li>
        <li><strong>A Medicare Advantage plan.</strong> Some Medicare Advantage plans offer extra benefits Original Medicare doesn’t cover, like vision, hearing or dental. Contact the plan for what is included. If you are weighing the two routes, read <a href="/medicare-advantage-vs-medigap">Medigap vs. Medicare Advantage</a>.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Common questions</h2>
      {faqs.map((f) => (<div class="mb-5"><h3 class="text-xl">{f.q}</h3><p>{f.a}</p></div>))}

      <div class="not-prose my-10 rounded-xl bg-crst-primary p-6 text-center">
        <p class="text-white font-heading text-lg mb-2 m-0">Want to talk through your options?</p>
        <p class="text-white/70 text-sm mb-4 m-0">A no-cost, no-pressure conversation, by phone or Zoom screen-share.</p>
        <a href={`tel:${BUSINESS.phoneClean}`} class="btn-accent text-base px-7 py-3">Call {BUSINESS.phone}</a>
      </div>

      <AuthorByline />

      <div class="not-prose mt-8">
        <Disclaimer variant="tpmo" />
        <p class="text-xs text-navy-500 mt-3 leading-relaxed">
          Medicare coverage rules are set by Medicare and can change. Plan availability, benefits and costs vary and are not guaranteed.
          This page is educational and not individualized advice. NY producer license #: {BUSINESS.nyLicense}.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>

  <CTASection headline="Let’s find the coverage that fits you" />
</BaseLayout>
